  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Monitoring Evaluation and Learning of Just Transitions for Water Security</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Just Transitions for Water Security Monitoring Evaluation and Learning (MEL) will independently review the performance and likely impact of the other four components namely the Water Resilience Tracker, Fair Water Footprints, Resilient Water Accelerator and Programme Management Support. It will also contribute to wider learning on &#x2018;what works&#x2019;.                                                                                                                    
 
The JTWS consortium will collaborate closely with The Monitoring, Evaluation and Learning service provider engaged by the FCDO to support this programme of work. The MEL lead will be responsible for overseeing successful delivery of programme MEL, tracking impacts, and working with consortium partners to ensure a learning centred programme following FCDO&#x2019;s best practice in adaptive management, and driven by the goal of transformative impact against a robust and well-tested theory of change. Engagement between the MEL service provider and the three workstreams will be coordinated through the Operational Coordination Unit (OCU) and Programme Executive Steering Committee (PESC). 

Progress towards the achievement of results will be monitored using the programme Theory of Change, the two programme-level ICF KPIs for resilience and transformational change and the four intermediate outcome level KPI&#x2019;s (national integrated, inclusive, and water resilient climate strategies and plans, water security indices, stewardship standards met and investable plans).  Deliverables will be set out in a results framework including key assumptions and verifiable milestones.</narrative>
  </description>
